# Prevents udisks2/gvfs from auto-mounting the ST-LINK/V2.1's own
# mass-storage LUN (NOD_F446RE) on the NUCLEO-F446RE board. That LUN is
# unused by this HIL flow (flashing goes over SWD via st-flash, not
# drag-and-drop), and the HIL runner power-cycles this exact USB port
# repeatedly and unattended -- an auto-mounted volume there is unwanted
# noise at best, and on the headless self-hosted CI host (no desktop
# session to grant mount permission) a source of friction, at worst.
#
# Matched via ATTRS{serial} (a plain sysfs attribute available
# immediately) rather than ENV{ID_SERIAL_SHORT} -- the latter is only
# populated later, by 60-persistent-storage.rules's IMPORT{builtin}=
# "usb_id", so a rule keyed on it here (evaluated earlier, by filename
# sort order) would never actually match. See
# infrastructure/udev/README.md for how this was diagnosed.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", ATTRS{serial}=="0669FF565271525067071140", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
